Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.090 align:start position:0%
 
I would have done probably four years in  prison for supervising sales reps  talking about our medical devices in a  way that didn't harm any patient howard  root is the CEO and founder of the  medical device company vascular  solutions which develops life-saving  medical technologies such as freeze dry  blood plasma to help wounded soldiers on  the battlefield and catheters that make  heart surgery safer and easier for  doctors but five years ago the Food and  Drug Administration filed a criminal  lawsuit against vascular solutions that  might have sent rout to prison for four  years while tearing apart the company he  spent decades building till we get this  top medical device companies aren't  gonna be started because no one's gonna  be crazy enough to do what I did 20  years ago today with this kind of  culture of prosecution against medical  device companies the dispute that almost  destroyed vascular solutions and landed  this 55 year old executive behind bars  involves the product they call the Vera  lace kit it uses lasers to treat  varicose veins which are not only a  cosmetic issue but also a health problem  that can lead to serious blood clotting  the agency accused root and his company  of selling medical devices without FDA  approval and then conspiring to hide  that fact we're in at litigious industry  so we get subpoenas once in a while but  this was a different subpoena because it  was a federal Department of Justice  subpoena and it was criminal  in 2010 the FDA approved the product for  use on veins near the surface of the  skin but not for veins that appear deep  under the flesh it's not that the agency  found evidence that the Vera lace kit  poses a significant danger when used in  this way it's just the agency didn't  specifically approve the device for this  purpose basically if they have  government's allegation is they're  making claims for which they've not  sought approval or clearance mark Duval  is an attorney who specializes in FDA  medical device compliance if the  government differs with you on the way  you're interpreting your labeling then  have a conversation with the company  maybe at worst write them a warning  letter but you don't indict them and  that's what was it at stake here in the  Howard brood vascular solutions case the  company applied for permission to market  the device for treating the short veins  that connect veins on the surface to  veins buried deep under the  skin these short veins are called  perforators but the application was  denied the FDA claims that vascular  solutions went ahead and marketed it for  this perforator vein use anyway even  developing a special attachment for the  vera lace kit specifically designed for  this purpose so the whole trial was on  this gray hub which we called the short  kit which was just a different version  of this other a standard 12 centimeter  kit so the government claimed that while  we could sell the red hub one that when  we sold the gray hub one that was  considered to be a crime but the FDA's  allegations regarding the grey hub tip  were false  in fact both the red hub and the gray  hub applicators can treat varicose veins  near the surface of the skin it's just  that many doctors chose to use the grey  tip to treat perforator veins as well  doctors didn't need the company's  permission to use the valets kit in this  way using medical devices in ways that  aren't specifically sanctioned by the  FDA which is known as off-label use is a  common and accepted practice government  doesn't progress medical practitioners  in the practice of medicine from doing  that they encourage it they know that  that's the way medicine gets advanced  you could not have cardiology procedures  on children unless you did off-label use  of medical devices because none of our  products are approved for the use on  patients under the age of 18 and  off-label use is recognized as being  legal necessary life-saving but  off-label promotion the government says  that's a crime the FDA charged the  company's sales team with encouraging  doctors to use the various kit for  off-label purposes a key piece of  evidence internal training materials in  which the FDA claimed company trainers  instructed salespeople to market the  product for use on the unapproved  perforator veins in fact these internal  presentations demonstrated no such thing  the presentations referred to doctors  using the device to treat short veins  but short veins are also found near the  surface of the skin and the company did  have FDA approval to market the device  for use near the surface of the skin  perforator veins are short short  saphenous vein is short there's a lot of  short segments and it's not a code word  for something illegal it's just a  description of a length of a vein that  you would treat with our prod  the government flagged an email route  forwarded to the entire Salesforce from  an employee bragging about selling the  kit to a doctor who mentioned that he  planned to use the device to treat  perforator veins noting that this would  alleviate the problem tenfold but  there's no evidence the salesperson was  pushing the doctor to use the device in  this way when they failed to find hard  evidence and internal company documents  US attorneys badgered employees at a  grand jury proceeding hoping to shape  their testimony into something usable I  quickly realized that the US government  is this monster of a thing that they  have all the power and all the money and  all the control and I felt very much  like a pawn with them the government  came back and not only asked for  clarification but stated that if I  didn't clarify it to what they wanted it  to say then certain things would happen  to me I couldn't lose my career I could  be charged and have to do jail time they  want you to sign this document  clarifying your testimony and I remember  reading the document and that's not what  I said and that's not what I intended to  say they wanted me to say I do not deny  that there was a conspiracy at the  company there was a document at one  point that I saw and there were four  current employees listed on there that  the government felt that these employees  had not been cooperative during the  process and were not probably a good  representation of what a company should  have especially in an officer level and  that those people should be terminated  and my name was on that list so they  tell the employees look we're getting  close to settling with the company and  when we settle with the company we're  gonna demand that they fire whoever  doesn't testify the way we want them to  testify so if you get on the right side  before the company settles you're good  if you're on the wrong side the company  will throw you under the bus and your  career will be over at this point the  Department of Justice was pouring time  and resources into destroying an  established medical device company and  fighting to put a well-regarded  executive behind bars  why because vascular solutions allegedly  encourage doctors to use a product in a  way that although it was benefiting  patients the agency hadn't okayed yet  of course that's not the whole story  this whole matter started as most of  these do with a whistleblower  so a disgruntled former employee decides  that he wants to start a complaint and  the system is set up so that the  whistleblower gets 20% of whatever the  government might recover from us in  pursuing his claim the Department of  Justice brags about its return on  investment for the dollar span they  claim that for every dollar they spend  and prosecutorial efforts they're  bringing $8 to the coffers vascular  solutions decided to settle the civil  suit for a little more than half a  million dollars a fraction of what it  would have cost the company to battle it  out in court although the government was  also willing to settle the criminal suit  root refused and insisted on going to  trial even though doing so meant risking  jail time we were fine if we had to pay  money we were fine if we had to do  compliance but we weren't going to take  employees who had done nothing wrong and  fire them and get them excluded from  anywhere in health care for their career  just to get out of this problem he  definitely could have gone to prison it  was risky to not settle the government's  case collapsed in the courtroom witness  after witness failed to back the  government side of the story the final  blow to the FDA's case came when an  expert witness called by the government  said that using the Verrill a skit on  perforator veins might not even qualify  as off-label use in some instances  undermining the entire premise of the  case one of the key governmental  witnesses basically testified on behalf  of the defense the defense rested  without calling a single witness from  its roster after five years and 25  million dollars in legal fees Howard  root walked free and vascular solutions  was in the clear with a not guilty  verdict the fight changed the way the  entire industry thinks about off-label  use and free speech the government by  acquiescing to a jury instruction agreed  that off-label promotion was not  necessarily illegal if it was wholly  truthful in improper context was her  shattering to the industry the evening  following his big win in court route  received a surprising email from one of  the jurors that said in all my life I've  never feared the government what the  federal government did to you your  company and your employ  is nothing short of criminal people say  you fear a jury  I didn't fear this jury I feared the  judge I really feared the prosecutors  but the jurors are the ones who really  know what's going on and they're the  ones who have justice in their hearts my  experience changed the way that I felt  about how the government is supposed to  protect the innocent and bring down the  bad guys bring down the people who are  truly doing criminal acts after watching  what I saw you know go on with the  prosecutors and how this played out and  how the information was manipulated I  don't think I could go into a courtroom  again and actually believe that the  government was telling the truth I will  never look at the US government the same  again route still worries about the  effect of overzealous regulation and  prosecution on medical innovation and  the health and lives of millions of  Americans what happens to medical device  companies affects the startups and we're  now bigger than the startups we're  substantial we're profitable and we can  continue to grow as long as we want to  but it's a sick feeling when you see not  as much development as it was 20 years  ago today because the government is  punishing people who are trying to start  new companies

